WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.267 --> 00:00:20.612
"Wait a minute!" Maggie said. "I thought the Valley High kids were innocent!"

2
00:00:20.613 --> 00:00:26.180
"Joey has an alibi since Melanie saw him at the restrooms," Henry replied.

3
00:00:26.181 --> 00:00:29.486
"And Tina seems too nice to be guilty.

4
00:00:29.487 --> 00:00:34.927
But William said the kids he saw sneaking around were wearing school T-shirts!"

5
00:00:34.928 --> 00:00:39.647
"Lots of people are wearing Belltown High shirts," Cole pointed out.

6
00:00:39.648 --> 00:00:43.139
"How do you know William meant Valley High ones?"

7
00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:47.943
"I don't," Henry said. "But we're out of other suspects.

8
00:00:47.944 --> 00:00:52.492
Maybe Tina and Joey are plotting against Belltown after all.

9
00:00:52.493 --> 00:00:55.192
She could have slashed those tires.

10
00:00:55.193 --> 00:01:00.648
And Joey could have hung around the restrooms to make sure nobody went down the trail and caught her."

11
00:01:00.649 --> 00:01:04.931
"Ooh! That's sneaky!" Maggie exclaimed.

12
00:01:04.932 --> 00:01:09.374
"Come on!" Henry cried. "Before we lose them!"

13
00:01:09.375 --> 00:01:16.551
The Lemonade Detectives took off, following the sounds of running feet and crunching leaves.

14
00:01:16.552 --> 00:01:21.133
Every once in a while they spotted a new flash of red and gold.

15
00:01:21.134 --> 00:01:24.865
But Henry still couldn't see who they were chasing.

16
00:01:24.866 --> 00:01:28.390
Finally they burst into a clearing.

17
00:01:28.391 --> 00:01:33.848
Two people were running across it, but only one of them was wearing a Valley High T-shirt.

18
00:01:33.849 --> 00:01:37.349
To Henry's surprise they were holding hands.

19
00:01:37.350 --> 00:01:41.881
"Stop!" Henry yelled. "We see you!"

20
00:01:41.882 --> 00:01:44.942
The two people dropped hands and spun around.

21
00:01:44.943 --> 00:01:47.854
"Leave us alone!" the boy yelled.

22
00:01:47.855 --> 00:01:50.978
"It's Joey!" Maggie exclaimed.

23
00:01:50.979 --> 00:01:54.801
Cole gasped. "And Melanie!"

24
00:01:54.802 --> 00:01:56.824
Henry was surprised too.

25
00:01:56.825 --> 00:02:01.118
What was the Belltown cheerleader doing with the Valley High bully?

26
00:02:01.119 --> 00:02:05.299
"Are you two boyfriend and girlfriend?" Maggie blurted out.

27
00:02:05.300 --> 00:02:08.991
"Please don't tell anyone!" Melanie begged.

28
00:02:08.992 --> 00:02:12.470
"My parents think I'm too young to have a boyfriend.

29
00:02:12.471 --> 00:02:18.639
Plus everyone at Belltown High will be mad if they know I'm dating someone from Valley High."

30
00:02:18.640 --> 00:02:21.433
Aha! Now Henry got it.

31
00:02:21.434 --> 00:02:27.846
"It was you, wasn't it?" he asked Joey. "You slashed those tires.

32
00:02:27.847 --> 00:02:32.459
Then you asked your secret girlfriend to provide your alibi!"

33
00:02:32.460 --> 00:02:37.855
Melanie gasped. "How did you know?" she cried.

34
00:02:37.856 --> 00:02:41.605
"I didn't until right now," Henry admitted.

35
00:02:41.606 --> 00:02:46.358
Maggie frowned. "Why did you slash everyone's tires?"

36
00:02:46.359 --> 00:02:51.630
"Those dumb kids from Belltown made me mad," Joey said with a scowl.

37
00:02:51.631 --> 00:02:55.204
"They said Valley High's sports teams were a joke!"

38
00:02:55.205 --> 00:03:00.166
Henry remembered hearing Tiny and his friends kidding around about that earlier in the day.

39
00:03:00.167 --> 00:03:04.354
"That's because you were picking on Nathan," he told Joey.

40
00:03:04.355 --> 00:03:08.809
"Anyway you still shouldn't have slashed anyone's tires."

41
00:03:08.810 --> 00:03:12.673
"It's all her fault," Joey muttered, pointing at Melanie.

42
00:03:12.674 --> 00:03:16.148
"She talked me into coming on this stupid bike ride."

43
00:03:16.149 --> 00:03:20.649
"What?" Melanie exclaimed. "How can you say that?

44
00:03:20.650 --> 00:03:23.680
I just wanted to spend time together!"

45
00:03:23.681 --> 00:03:26.058
Now Henry understood everything.

46
00:03:26.059 --> 00:03:29.330
Melanie's parents wouldn't let her go out with Joey.

47
00:03:29.331 --> 00:03:34.373
So she'd talked Joey into coming to the bike ride so they could be together in secret.

48
00:03:34.374 --> 00:03:38.637
That's why William had seen them sneaking away a few times during the ride.

49
00:03:38.638 --> 00:03:43.993
But then Joey had ruined everything by losing his temper and slashing the tires.

50
00:03:43.994 --> 00:03:52.887
"Whatever," Joey muttered. "You guys better not tell anyone, or else!"

51
00:03:52.888 --> 00:03:56.517
"Or else what?" a deep voice asked.

52
00:03:56.518 --> 00:04:03.968
It was Chuck the bodyguard! He'd just stepped into the clearing.

53
00:04:03.969 --> 00:04:07.385
Joey looked surprised. "Who are you?"

54
00:04:07.386 --> 00:04:12.912
"I'm the person who's going to make sure that you pay for those slashed tires."

55
00:04:12.913 --> 00:04:15.306
Chuck grabbed Joey by the arm.

56
00:04:15.307 --> 00:04:20.497
"Come on, kid. You too, blondie," he added, glancing at Melanie.

57
00:04:20.498 --> 00:04:26.332
"Yes, sir," she said meekly, scurrying along as Chuck dragged Joey away.

58
00:04:26.333 --> 00:04:28.794
Watching the scene, Maggie grinned.

59
00:04:28.795 --> 00:04:32.515
"I guess that's another case closed," she said.

60
00:04:32.516 --> 00:04:38.720
"The Lemonade Detectives keep their perfect record!"

61
00:04:38.721 --> 00:04:44.325
The next day at the lemonade stand, Henry and his friends were still talking about the case.

62
00:04:44.326 --> 00:04:47.827
"I heard Melanie broke up with Joey," Cole said.

63
00:04:47.828 --> 00:04:51.980
"Good," Maggie said. "He's not very nice."

64
00:04:51.981 --> 00:04:56.169
"I'm glad he'll have to pay for those tires," Henry said.

65
00:04:56.170 --> 00:05:02.756
"That means the soccer team gets to keep all the money they raised."

66
00:05:02.757 --> 00:05:05.428
Henry noticed William hurrying toward them.

67
00:05:05.429 --> 00:05:09.750
"Hi," William said. "I heard I'd find you guys here."

68
00:05:09.751 --> 00:05:13.072
"Want some lemonade?" Maggie poured some into a cup.

69
00:05:13.073 --> 00:05:15.535
"For you, it's on the house."

70
00:05:15.536 --> 00:05:18.271
"Thanks." William took a sip.

71
00:05:18.272 --> 00:05:21.117
"I'm on my way to Nathan's house to hang out.

72
00:05:21.118 --> 00:05:24.911
But I wanted to stop and thank you again for being so friendly to me."

73
00:05:24.912 --> 00:05:30.405
"You're welcome," Henry said. "Tell Chuck thanks again for his help.

74
00:05:30.406 --> 00:05:36.788
If he hadn't come along when he did, Joey might have decided to beat us up to keep us quiet."

75
00:05:36.789 --> 00:05:41.450
"He's just glad you kept our secret," William said. "And guess what?

76
00:05:41.451 --> 00:05:46.780
He helped me convince my parents that I don't need a bodyguard for most of the stuff I do around town!"

77
00:05:46.781 --> 00:05:51.961
"That's great." Henry smiled, glad that William seemed happier.

78
00:05:51.962 --> 00:05:57.217
"Don't worry, you can tell them that Belltown is a pretty safe place."

79
00:05:57.218 --> 00:05:59.294
"Yeah." Cole grinned.

80
00:05:59.295 --> 00:06:07.250
"Especially with The Lemonade Detectives always on the job!"
